[16:30:16] The story is complete. Summary:
[16:30:16] **The defect.** `IconSync.referencedOrUnknownItemIds` selected `FROM items`, so an item id account synchronization had stored but for which no metadata row was ever created was *structurally* unreachable — exactly the gap `STORY-API-009` recorded.
[16:30:16] **What changed** (`src/main/java/sync/IconSync.java`, its test class, one live-check script):
[16:30:16] - Selection is now a union of the reference families themselves (bank, materials, character inventories, recipe outputs, recipe ingredients) plus `items WHERE icon_url IS NULL` — no tradeability join, so nontradeables are covered.
[16:30:16] - The write became an upsert: a missing row is **created** with canonical `name`/`type`/`rarity`/`vendor_value`/`icon_url`/`fetched_at`; an existing row keeps every value and has only `icon_url` updated, and only when upstream supplied one *and* it differs. `items.icon_path` is still never touched.
[16:30:16] - A failed batch is reported and skipped, not fatal; a `MetadataRepair` report classifies unresolved ids (not returned / no icon / rejected source / failed batch).
[16:30:16] **Real-database repair**, executed against the actual user data (metadata only, no account sync):
[16:30:16] | | before | after |
[16:30:16] |---|---|---|
[16:30:16] | occupied bank slots with an icon source | 75 / 163 | **163 / 163** |
[16:30:16] | material stacks | 678 / 680 | **680 / 680** |
[16:30:16] | recipe ingredients | 2 870 / 2 873 | **2 873 / 2 873** |
[16:30:16] | recipe outputs | 12 975 / 13 065 | **13 025 / 13 065** |
[16:30:16] | character items with no `items` row | 216 | **0** |
[16:30:16] 297 rows created. An immediate second run wrote **0 rows**. The 40 remaining are recipe outputs the GW2 API answers `no such id` for — unresolvable, not pending, and still selected next run.
[16:30:16] **Tests run:** `IconSyncMetadataTest` 14/14 (disposable Postgres schema, controlled upstream fixture); `sync.*Test` 35/35; `ItemIconApiRealDbIT` 3/3 printing `163 with an accepted retained icon source` where API-009 printed 74. Live: `icon-live-check.mjs` extended to Bank/Materials/Profit — `pre-restart` PASSED 7 steps with **0 entries without metadata and 0 failed on all three views**, `post-restart` PASSED 4 steps with 0 upstream tunnels, `smoke:account` PASSED 8 steps with 505 images and 0 fallbacks. The isolated cache started empty and ended with 312 files built at runtime; the user's cache was never touched.
[16:30:16] One honest note: my first `post-restart` run **failed** because the added navigations moved the upstream-tunnel count out of the window that phase asserts about — I fixed the script and reran both phases.
[16:30:16] Two follow-up findings recorded (F001: §12.1 does not contain the metadata-coverage requirement Request-009's resolution claims it was given; F002: a timing race in `account-browser-smoke.mjs`'s bank-reload step). Docs updated at their owners: `CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` §5.14 and `KNOWN_PROBLEMS.md` KP-22, the latter marked partially resolved — metadata half only, with the JavaFX rendering and stale-path halves left explicitly open.
