[16:40:31] Done. The deficiency is fixed.
[16:40:31] ## What changed
[16:40:31] **`src/main/java/sync/IconSync.java`** — the metadata upsert's conflict branch. It previously wrote only `icon_url` on an existing row, so a row that existed but held no canonical metadata stayed empty even when upstream returned it:
[16:40:31] ```sql
[16:40:31] ON CONFLICT (item_id) DO UPDATE SET
[16:40:31]   name         = COALESCE(items.name, EXCLUDED.name),
[16:40:31]   type         = COALESCE(items.type, EXCLUDED.type),
[16:40:31]   rarity       = COALESCE(items.rarity, EXCLUDED.rarity),
[16:40:31]   vendor_value = COALESCE(items.vendor_value, EXCLUDED.vendor_value),
[16:40:31]   icon_url     = COALESCE(EXCLUDED.icon_url, items.icon_url)
[16:40:31] WHERE (EXCLUDED.icon_url IS NOT NULL AND items.icon_url IS DISTINCT FROM EXCLUDED.icon_url)
[16:40:31]    OR (items.name IS NULL AND EXCLUDED.name IS NOT NULL)
[16:40:31]    OR … (type, rarity, vendor_value)
[16:40:31] ```
[16:40:31] Each canonical field coalesces stored-side-first, so a populated value is never overwritten; `icon_url` coalesces the other way so a response without an icon still cannot blank a stored source. The widened `WHERE` is what makes the filled values actually persist while keeping an unchanged run at zero row updates.
[16:40:31] ## Tests
[16:40:31] `anExistingRowMissingCanonicalFieldsHasThemFilledWithoutOverwritingWhatItHolds` — an existing bank-referenced row with all four canonical fields NULL plus a second row with a populated name; asserts the NULLs are filled, the stored name/`icon_url`/`icon_path` survive, `rowsCreated=0`, and a repeat run writes 0 rows. I temporarily restored the old statement to confirm it fails there: `both half-populated rows were completed ==> expected: <2> but was: <0>`.
[16:40:31] The pre-existing changed-source test seeded canonically incomplete rows, which would have made its "only the changed item is written" assertion vacuous; its two rows are now complete so the assertion still means what it says.
[16:40:31] - `./mvnw -o test -Dtest=IconSyncMetadataTest -DfailIfNoTests=false` → `Tests run: 15, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0`
[16:40:31] - `./mvnw -o test -Dtest='sync.*Test'` → `Tests run: 36, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0`
[16:40:31] ## Real-database re-run
[16:40:31] Ran the documented standalone invocation again against the real database: `--dry-run` reported 14 302 selected / 40 without a row, the run reported `rowsWritten=0, rowsCreated=0, notReturnedUpstream=40, batchesFailed=0`. A throwaway read-only reporter (deleted) showed 0 `items` rows missing any canonical field both before and after. So the widened write causes no churn, and — honestly stated — this database holds no half-populated row today, so the completion path itself is evidenced by the targeted test rather than by live data. That limit is recorded in the story, the result and §5.14.
[16:40:31] Docs updated at their owner: `CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` §5.14 (write table row + evidence paragraph), story Result/Status, `CLAUDE_RESULT.md`, the single BACKLOG entry, and a new `tasks/lessons.md` rule about conflict branches that create a full row but complete nothing. Follow-up findings F001/F002 are unchanged.
